    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Right-click $(l)any part$() of the core to open its screen: the pedestal, any cell of the shell (finished or not) or any block of a pylon column lined up with it. The screen shows:",
      "title": "The screen"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)its $(l)tier and shell$(), and whether it is $(l)Online$() (working) or $(l)Unstable$() (too few pylon columns, so nothing goes in or out);$(br)$(li)the pylon columns it has and needs (point at the line for what this tier asks for);"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)what it found on each side$(): a linked pylon, or why one does not count (no pylon, too close, too far, too short, beam blocked). Point at a side for the column's height and distance;$(br)$(li)how much each pylon carries, and the FE stored."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)1$(): none, 1,000,000 FE, 1, 2, 3-8, 16,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)2$(): 3x3x3 (26 cells), 32,000,000 FE, 2, 3, 4-10, 128,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)3$(): 5x5x5 (98 cells), 256,000,000 FE, 3, 4, 5-12, 512,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)4$(): 7x7x7 (218 cells), 2,000,000,000 FE, 4, 5, 6-14, 2,000,000 FE/t",
      "title": "Numbers"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Column height is the least a column needs. Distance is counted in blocks from the pedestal."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)Breaking a cell of the shell drops the core back a tier, and $(l)the energy that no longer fits is lost$(). Empty the core before you rebuild it.$(br)$(li)Breaking the pedestal leaves the shell's cells where they are, visible again, but $(l)all the energy stored is lost$().",
      "title": "Tips"
    },
